-- title:
--   Gauss valuation as the only such valuation subring of K
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and an integer $M \neq 0$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $p$-th root of unity, and let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((q))$ obtained as [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField M)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the field generated over $L$ inside the Laurent series field by the coefficientwise images under $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_1(M)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ (the field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldC ℚ (Gamma1 M)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L134)). Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A \to L$, and assume $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A \to L \to K$. Let $j \in K$ be the element whose underlying Laurent series is the coefficientwise image in $L((q))$ of $\mathrm{jq} = q^{-1}\,\mathrm{jNum}(q)$, with $j \neq 0$. Let $V$ be a valuation subring of $K$ such that the image of $A$ lies in $V$, the image of the maximal ideal of $A$ consists of non-units of $V$, and for every $P \in A[X]$ whose reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ is nonzero both $P(j)$ and $P(j)^{-1}$ lie in $V$. Then for every $f \in K$ one has $f \in V$ if and only if there are power series $x, y \in A[[q]]$ with $y$ of nonzero reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ such that $f \cdot y = x$ in $L((q))$, the power series being viewed in $L((q))$ via $A \to L$.
--
--   This is good reduction of $X_1(M)$ at a prime $p \nmid M$ in valuation form: the Gauss valuation of the $j$-line, whose valuation ring consists of the quotients $x/y$ of power series over $A$ with $y$ of nonzero reduction, is the only valuation subring of the function field $K$ of $X_1(M)$ over $L$ that dominates $A$ and contains the inverses of all polynomials in $j$ with nonzero reduction; equivalently, the special fibre of the normalisation of the $j$-line over $A$ in $K$ is irreducible. It is used in the computation of the degree of $K$ over $L(j)$ in terms of the corresponding degree over $\mathbb{Q}$, in the primality of the ideal generated by the uniformiser in the integral $j$-finite chart, and in the separability statement for residue fields in the level-raising comparison between $X_1(M)$ and $X_1(Mp)$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneP_mem_valuationSubring_iff_exists_powerSeries_of_x1.lean

